Package: biasProxyR
Title: Sampling Effort Proxies for Species Distribution Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Aamna", "Naveed", , "naamna588@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0001-3371-1066"))
Description: Addresses geographic sampling bias in species distribution 
    models for data-poor regions. It generates sampling effort proxies 
    using open-source infrastructure data, allowing researchers to sample 
    bias-aware background points. This prevents models from learning 
    sampling artifacts instead of true ecological niches. The spatial data 
    processing relies on methods described in Hijmans (2025) 
    <doi:10.32614/CRAN.package.terra> and Pebesma (2018) 
    <doi:10.32614/CRAN.package.sf>.
